The pumping and surface extension adds 38 learning Records and three sources. Displacement/dry, gas-ballast, Roots, liquid-ring, vapor-jet, turbomolecular, cryogenic, getter and ion-pump mechanisms lead into finite compression, foreline/exhaust and complete selection. Surfaces develop explicit inventories, residence/coverage, binding-state distributions, readsorption, atomic/molecular diffusion, finite slabs, permeation/time lag, surface recombination, virtual leaks, joints, material state, cleaning, thermal history and measurement. A primary chamber comparison, stimulated desorption and molecular heat transfer connect the mechanisms to research. An original network program leads into three advanced investigations of complete pumping, competing gas sources and manufactured surface function; these converge at `gas-pumps-review` (`r_5QS86VWMREAY4AADFCSZEB5XKQ`). Its continuation now develops storage/distribution.

