Independent checks in `/tmp/check-gases-delivery-physics.py` passed 119 numerical comparisons plus bounds and limiting-case assertions. They include 60-digit inventory arithmetic; nine separately integrated ideal-gas withdrawal/energy cases; filling closure; conductivity-integral quadrature for five laws, a monotonicity bound and a counterexample without monotonicity; heat/boil-off/reserve arithmetic; choked-flow maxima and independent Mach-state mass flux for three heat-capacity ratios; continuous purge with source and removal closure in both the dilute-trace approximation and the exact added-gas model; pressure-cycle component conservation; four two-volume analytical/eigenvalue solutions compared with independent RK4 integration and impurity closure; buffer arithmetic; and two independently integrated isothermal pressure-loss cases. The purge Record explicitly distinguishes an added-gas source, which changes outlet flow at constant inventory, from the trace approximation or replacement of carrier gas. These verify the explicit ideal models and rounded examples, not actual equipment ratings or experimental performance. No new inline program, application feature or Rust code was added in this extension. Do not rerun the draft/publication scripts: the authored purge Records now include this later refinement.

