The original pump/refill model explicitly distinguishes impurity fraction in a partly evacuated vessel from fraction after pure-gas refill. With constant molar ingress and species-independent pumping, final composition approaches a floor; lower pressure alone does not determine an optimal stopping time. The study asks readers to define the objective and test the paper's installation-specific inference. `/tmp/check-gases-operations-physics.py` passed 122 independent numerical comparisons plus exact component conservation, probability and state bounds: room mixing, availability versus uninterrupted reliability, common-cause events, exact interval-average hidden failure, no-failure Poisson bounds, part-load power, conditional helium yields and component-wise pump/refill balances. ODE integration, probability enumeration, quadrature and high-precision arithmetic check the explicit teaching models independently.

